---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Seven channels, one a week: acoustic, electrical, timing,
    electromagnetic, cache, optical, thermal. Each week you read the
    disclosure that established the channel is real, then work with a
    captured trace, a decay curve, a threat model or a piece of code written
    to leak (or not to). The remaining weeks turn that list into something
    usable — a rubric that scores the channels, a discipline for closing one,
    and a design review: given a device and an adversary, say which channels
    apply, in what order, and what closing each one actually costs.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who wants to know what a machine reveals about its computation
    without being asked. No electronics or cryptography background is assumed — the course builds the arithmetic and
    circuitry it needs as each channel requires it. What it does assume is
    patience for a slow, cumulative argument: each week only makes sense
    against the ones before it.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title="Lectures" href="/lectures/">
      <p>
        The twelve-week argument, one line per week, and the lecture behind
        each line.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly measurement work: what you read, capture or rewrite.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
